## Prerequisites
- OpenAI API key with access to Realtime models (`OPENAI_API_KEY`)
- Node.js 18+ (for the TypeScript/JS SDK) or Python 3.9+
- If migrating from Realtime API Beta: read the [migration guide](https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/realtime-migration) — the beta endpoint was removed May 12, 2026

## Install the SDK

```bash
# Node.js / TypeScript
npm install openai

# Python
pip install openai
```

## Basic Realtime 2 session (TypeScript)

```typescript
import OpenAI from 'openai';

const client = new OpenAI({ apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY });

// Create a Realtime session
const session = await client.beta.realtime.sessions.create({
  model: 'realtime-2',       // Realtime 2 model
  voice: 'alloy',
  instructions: 'You are a helpful assistant. Answer concisely.',
  turn_detection: { type: 'server_vad' },
  // Enable reasoning (trades latency for accuracy)
  reasoning: { effort: 'medium' },
});

console.log('Session created:', session.id);
console.log('Client secret:', session.client_secret.value);
// Use client_secret to authenticate WebSocket from the browser/client
```

## WebSocket connection (browser-side)

```typescript
// Use the ephemeral client_secret from the session above
const ws = new WebSocket(
  'wss://api.openai.com/v1/realtime',
  ['realtime', `openai-insecure-api-key.${session.client_secret.value}`, 'openai-beta.realtime-v2']
);

ws.onopen = () => {
  // Send audio input as base64 PCM16 24kHz
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({
    type: 'input_audio_buffer.append',
    audio: base64EncodedPCM16Audio,
  }));
};

ws.onmessage = (event) => {
  const msg = JSON.parse(event.data);
  if (msg.type === 'response.audio.delta') {
    // msg.delta is base64 PCM16 audio — pipe to your audio output
    playAudio(msg.delta);
  }
};
```

## Realtime Translate (streaming speech translation)

```typescript
// Same session create, different model surface
const translateSession = await client.beta.realtime.sessions.create({
  model: 'realtime-translate',
  // Translate from Spanish to English
  input_language: 'es',
  output_language: 'en',
  voice: 'alloy',
});
```

## Realtime Whisper (streaming transcription only)

```typescript
const transcribeSession = await client.beta.realtime.sessions.create({
  model: 'realtime-whisper',
  input_language: 'en',  // null for auto-detect
});
// Response events will be response.transcript.delta instead of response.audio.delta
```

## Gotchas
- **Realtime API Beta is gone** — the old `wss://api.openai.com/v1/realtime?model=gpt-4o-realtime-preview` endpoint was removed May 12. Update your model string to `realtime-2` and review the [migration guide](https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/realtime-migration)
- **Audio format is PCM16 24kHz** — not MP3, not Opus; encode/decode accordingly on both ends
- **Reasoning increases first-audio latency** — with `effort: 'high'`, expect ~500–800ms before first audio chunk; use `effort: 'low'` for conversational applications where speed matters more than depth
- **Voice options affect audio quality** — OpenAI's release notes flag occasional pitch/tone variations with certain voices; test your chosen voice under load before production
